{"name":"Coffee Whip","hex":"#df9d5b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"coffee","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A beverage made by infusing the beans of the coffee plant in hot water. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A serving of this beverage."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a pale brown colour, like that of milk coffee.","Of a table: a small, low table suitable for people in lounge seating to put coffee cups on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coffee"},{"term":"whip","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A lash; a pliant, flexible instrument, such as a rod (commonly of cane or rattan) or a plaited or braided rope or thong (commonly of leather) used to create a sharp \"crack\" sound for directing or herding animals.","The same instrument used to strike a person or animal for corporal punishment or torture."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hit with a whip.","To hit with any flexible object."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whip"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coffee","blocks":[{"text":"Coffee is a beverage brewed from roasted, ground coffee beans. Dark-colored and bitter, coffee has a stimulating effect on humans due to its caffeine content; however decaffeinated coffee is also commercially available. There are also various coffee substitutes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Latte_and_dark_coffee.jpg/330px-Latte_and_dark_coffee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffee"},{"title":"Whip","blocks":[{"text":"A whip is a blunt weapon or implement used in a striking motion to create sound or pain. Whips can be used for flagellation against humans or animals to exert control or strength through pain compliance or fear of pain, or be used as an audible cue through the distinct whipcrack effect. Whips are commonly used on horses to give subtle cues as tapping. The portion of the whip used for striking is generally either a firm rod designed for direct contact, or a flexible line requiring a specialized swinging motion. The former is easier and more precise, the latter offers longer reach and greater force. Some varieties have an extended stock section in addition to the line."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Riding_crop.jpeg/330px-Riding_crop.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whip"},{"title":"Coffee (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Coffee is a brownish color that is a representation of a roasted coffee bean. Different types of coffee beans have different colors when roasted—the color coffee represents an average."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffee_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Coffee_beans_unroasted.jpg/500px-Coffee_beans_unroasted.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Coffee_beans_unroasted.jpg/1280px-Coffee_beans_unroasted.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Coffee_beans_unroasted.jpg/500px-Coffee_beans_unroasted.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Green coffee describes the beans before roasting.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACoffee_beans_unroasted.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/The_Vertue_of_the_COFFEE_Drink.jpg/330px-The_Vertue_of_the_COFFEE_Drink.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia